P4 (#945): content + contacts adapter framework

Ships the adapter framework needed to drain the 149 P4-tagged
dispatch-allowlist entries (task #938).

Content (`supabase/functions/_shared/execution/adapters/content/`):
- types.ts — domain enum, allowlisted write tables, payload validators
- policy.ts — per-row + per-pipeline lock + idempotency keys (FNV-1a)
- row-repository.ts — DI seam over generic table CRUD
- content-row-adapter.ts — generic per-row adapter (insert/update/
  upsert/delete) registered as NON_CRITICAL_DATA_FIX with auto
  rollback via snapshot
- bulk-pipeline-adapter.ts — factory producing food/search/shop/media
  bulk adapters as NON_SENSITIVE_BULK_UPDATE with manual rollback;
  no-op runners ship registered with loud warnings, NO_COMPENSATING_RUN
  if no compensator (no silent rollback success)
- content-verifier.ts — row + bulk verifiers
- bootstrap.ts — registers verifiers first, adapters with overwrite,
  reconciles against system.agents (prod throws, dev warns)

Contacts (`supabase/functions/_shared/execution/adapters/contacts/`):
- types.ts — sync + upsert payloads, CONTACTS_TABLE_ALLOWLIST
- policy.ts — per-provider + per-(table,source) locks
- contacts-repository.ts — upsertMany + countWhere DI seam
- contacts-adapter.ts — sync + upsert adapters, both registered as
  NON_SENSITIVE_BULK_UPDATE, manual rollback via per-provider /
  per-source compensators (NO_COMPENSATING_RUN otherwise)
- contacts-verifier.ts — sync rows-affected + upsert count verifiers
- bootstrap.ts — same shape as content bootstrap; ships no-op runners
  for all 17 P4 sync providers

Wiring (`supabase/functions/execution-loop/index.ts`):
- imports both bootstraps inside `ensureAdaptersBootstrapped`
- new `isAgentContentEnabled()` / `isAgentContactsEnabled()` helpers
  read AGENT_CONTENT_ENABLED / AGENT_CONTACTS_ENABLED env flags
- when a flag is OFF the bootstrap is skipped (and a console.warn
  fires) — tasks then fail loudly with NO_ADAPTER. No silent fallback
  to direct mutation.

Docs:
- `docs/audits/agent-migration/p4-content-contacts.md` — phase plan
  documenting scope, flags, drain gate, and §6 mechanical drain
  command for task #938

Sub-domains chosen so registry keys stay unique while sharing the
canonical task types from src/core/execution/risk-classification.ts:
content.row | content.food/search/shop/media | contacts.sync/upsert.

